# HTTP headers applied by Cloudflare Workers' static-asset serving.
# Vite copies `public/_headers` verbatim into `dist/`.
#
# HOW MULTIPLE MATCHING RULES COMBINE (important — got us burned once):
# Cloudflare Workers Assets APPENDS the headers of *every* matching rule; it
# does NOT do "most specific wins". A request for `/embed` matches both `/*`
# and `/embed`, so it receives BOTH Content-Security-Policy headers, and the
# browser enforces the INTERSECTION (most restrictive) of all CSPs present.
# Consequence: a `frame-ancestors` on `/*` can never be *loosened* by a more
# specific rule — the intersection keeps the strict value. So `frame-ancestors`
# is NOT set on `/*`; it is set per document: `'self'` on the app pages, `*` on
# `/embed`. (A CSP that omits `frame-ancestors` imposes no framing limit, so
# the per-document value is the one that takes effect.)
#
# CSP notes:
#   - `script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'` — no 'unsafe-inline' / 'unsafe-eval'.
#     'wasm-unsafe-eval' is what DuckDB-WASM needs to compile its modules; Vega
#     renders through the vega-interpreter AST evaluator (see ChartVisualizer)
#     so it needs no 'unsafe-eval'. The `/*` rule also allows
#     static.cloudflareinsights.com for the analytics beacon; the `/embed`
#     policy intersects it away (no beacon there).
#   - `worker-src 'self' blob:` — DuckDB-WASM's workers.
#   - `connect-src … https:` — datasets / the DuckDB-WASM .wasm.
#   - `style-src 'unsafe-inline'` — the inline <style> in index/embed.html plus
#     styles Vega / CodeMirror inject at runtime.
#   - `frame-ancestors` MUST be an HTTP header (the CSP spec disallows it from
#     <meta>).

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https: blob: data:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'

# Main-app documents forbid framing (clickjacking defense-in-depth). Listed per
# path because `frame-ancestors` can't live on `/*` (see the header note above).
# `/demo` is a real route (BedevereApp reads `location.pathname === "/demo"`).
# NOTE: arbitrary SPA-fallback URLs (e.g. /anything → index.html) are NOT
# covered here and stay framable — a small residual gap; a headers-setting
# Worker is the follow-up that closes it fully.
/
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
/index.html
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
/demo
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'

# /embed is the public, read-only embeddable widget — framable by any origin.
/embed
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; worker-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https: blob: data:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors *
/embed.html
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; worker-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https: blob: data:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors *
